{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumClique()"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically least largest clique by vertex index, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored. Each largest clique is searched for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from its first vertex v in degeneracy order, among v’s later neighbors, so memory stays O(n +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"m + degeneracy²) however large a hub’s degree; of two cliques of one size, the lesser is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one holding the least vertex of their symmetric difference. For each v, a witness clique W"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(any one of the right size) guides a pass over the candidates in ascending number: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"candidate in W is taken, any other is taken exactly when a search finds the rest of a clique"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"among the common neighbors left (which then becomes W). A v whose candidates all exceed the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least vertex of the best clique so far is skipped. Exponential in the worst case."}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumClique"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"